}
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
p { margin: 4px 0 10px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 284)</h2>
<p><b>Everyone sees the same crop — zoom and pan now travel.</b></p>
<ul>
<li>Zoom and pan are shared: when you punch in on a detail, native guests and web reviewers land on the same crop, centered on the same point — expressed relative to fit, so it reads correctly on any screen size. The web zooms with the scroll wheel (at the cursor) and fits with F, and driving works both ways.</li>
<li>Comments and drawings now carry which clip they belong to. Anything applied late — a mailbox pickup, a late join — files into the right clip instead of whichever was on screen; messages for a clip that hasn't loaded yet wait and attach when it arrives.</li>
<li>Web clip switching is solid: switching into a clip that already has marks no longer breaks the page (the exact "clip list disconnected / timeline dead" report), and a failed switch rolls back cleanly instead of leaving a dead player.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
